  "uprn": "200002814705",
  "decision_date": "31/03/2006",
  "description": "Erection of one part 2-storey, part 3-storey and part 4-storey block and one part 2-storey, part 3-storey block together comprising 45 two-bedroom flats with 63 parking spaces and associated amenity areas.",
  "site_name": "Greenham Park",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "03/04/2006",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": "Chertsey Road",
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Major dwellings",
  "lapsed_date": "30/03/2009",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The proposed redevelopment of the site for housing would be compatible with the character of the area and would not detract from the open aspect or visual amenities of the Green Belt. The proposal would not result in unacceptable harm to neighbours' living conditions, would provide acceptable living conditions for future occupiers and would not result in conditions prejudicial to highway and pedestrian safety. The proposal complies with adopted Unitary Development Plan policies ENV-B.1.1 (New Development), ENV-N.1.4 (Development near the Green Belt Boundary), E.1.5 (Development involving loss or changes in employment generating uses), H.1.1 (Location of New Housing Development), H.4.1 (Housing Standards and Guidelines), H.2.1 (Affordable Housing), H.4.2 (Residential Density) and T.1.4 (Car and Cycle Parking and Servicing Facilities For Developments).",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - No development shall take place until samples of the materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the hereby permitted have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details",
    "Condition : 4 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 5 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8am-6pm Mondays to Friday and 8am-1pm Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - The use hereby permitted shall not be begun until details of the arrangements for storing of waste and recycled materials have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The arrangements for storing waste and recycled materials shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with any approval given and shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 7 - Before the development is commenced a scheme for protecting the proposed residential accommodation from excessive external noise shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority and any works which form part of such a scheme shall be completed before any part of the development is first occupied or used.",
    "Condition : 8 - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority and these works shall be carried out as approved.  These details shall include proposed finished levels or contours; means of enclosure; car parking layouts; other vehicle and pedestrian access and circulation areas; hard surfacing material; minor artefacts and structures (eg. furniture, play equipment, refuse or other storage units, signs, lighting etc).\r\n\r\nSoft landscape works shall include (planting plans; written specifications (including cultivation and other operations associated with plant and grass establishment); schedules of plants, noting species, plant sizes and proposed numbers/densities where appropriate; implementation programme).",
    "Condition : 9 - All hard and soft landscape works shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.  The works shall be carried out prior to the occupation of any part of the development or in accordance with the programme agreed with the local planning authority",
    "Condition : 10 - No development shall take place until there has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority a plan indicating the positions, design, materials and type of boundary treatment to be erected.  The boundary treatment shall be completed before the dwellings are occupied or in accordance with a timetable agreed in writing with the local planning authority.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 11 - A landscape management plan, including long term design objectives, management responsibilities and maintenance schedules for all hard and soft landscape areas, shall be submitted to and approved by the local planning authority prior to the occupation of the development or any phase of the development, whichever is the sooner, for its permitted use.  The landscape management plan shall be carried out as approved.",
    "Condition : 12 - No development shall take place until a schedule of landscape maintenance for a minimum period of 5 years has been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.  The schedule shall include details of the arrangements for its implementation.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved schedule.",
    "Condition : 13 - Before first occupation of the buildings the access, turning and parking spaces (including spaces for people with disabilities) shall be provided within the curtilage of the site in accordance with the scheme shown on drawing No. M04/367/50 Rev B and such spaces shall be permanently available and not be used for any other purpose.",
    "Condition : 14 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site\r\n\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 15 - Before the development hereby permitted is commenced a scheme indicating the provision to be made for disabled people to gain access to the buildings and parking spaces shall have been submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority.  The agreed scheme shall be implemented before the development hereby permitted is brought into use.",
    "Condition : 16 - Landfill site:\r\n\r\nBefore the development hereby permitted commences:\r\na.\tThe site shall be investigated by a competent person to identify the extent and nature of contamination. A detailed site investigation report shall be prepared and submitted to the LPA for comment.  The report should include a tiered risk assessment of the contamination based on the proposed end use of the site.\r\n\r\nb.\tA scheme for decontamination of the site shall be submitted to the LPA, for written approval.\r\n\r\nBefore the development hereby permitted is first occupied:\r\n\r\nc.\tThe LPA shall be notified immediately if additional contamination is discovered during the course of the development. A competent person shall assess the additional contamination, and shall submit appropriate amendments to the scheme for decontamination in writing to the LPA for approval. \r\n\r\nd.\tThe agreed scheme for decontamination, including amendments, must be fully implemented and a written validation (closure) report submitted to the LPA for approval.",
    "Condition : 17 - The construction of the foul and surface discharge drainage system shall be carried out in accordance with details submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the development commences.",
    "Condition : 18 - No soakaways shall be constructed in contaminated ground.",
    "Condition : 19 - ."
  ],
